    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VncZsisuSw6LY8LZia9364)_\n\nFollows #271 and #272. With the config in `~/dotfiles` and linked by Stow, Magit works through `vc-follow-symlinks`; this removes what only yadm needed.\n\n- `vc-follow-symlinks` is set once, by `sp-auto-follow-symlinks` in `sp-navi` (called from `sp-helper-funct`). The duplicate `setq` from #272 is removed from `sp-vcontrol`, and its doc points at `sp-navi`.\n- `sp-network`: the `yadm` TRAMP method is removed (the module keeps `plz`).\n- `GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES` is removed from the `sp-env` list and from the fish config.\n- `sp-org-issues`: the `sp-org-issues-yadm-repo` option and the Magit hook that showed untracked files in yadm worktrees are removed; a normal repo needs neither.\n- Docs: treemacs commentary, `emacs-pr` text in the README (`git` in `~/dotfiles`, new package path), load-order table, sandbox table, root README row, projects-sidebar note. CHANGELOG entry added.\n\nLeft as they are: the names `sp-yadm-repo` (now `~/dotfiles/.git` when it exists) and the `yadm` source of the config agenda view, because renaming them touches `sp-org-issues`, its tests and your customisations.\n\nNot run in Emacs (none in the container); parentheses of the changed `.el` files were checked by a script, and the `tangle` check is the real test for the `.el`/doc match.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCrRWec3LtT3WLhGCc)_",
